        "id": 1013030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-19T17:58:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I guess you mean it can be triggered by a malicious userspace. You could send a BC_CLEAR_DEATH_NOTIFICATION (which adds to thread-\u003etodo) without reading from the kernel, which leaves it in the thread-\u003etodo, and then initiate a transaction. Perhaps there are legitimate scenarios too. Will think about this more.",
      "parentUuid": "0fe71dea_db34163d",
      "revId": "34c3493e45451d505d05c52266e946fbb592c001",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ecff026_58b19e4a",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3289,
      "author": {
        "id": 1013030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-19T19:17:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So from what I can tell, the current driver only queues to thread-\u003etodo (from the local process) in the following scenarios:\n- userspace sends BC_REQUEST_DEATH_NOTIFICATION, but we have no memory for the death recipient\n- userspace sends BC_CLEAR_DEATH_NOTIFICATION (for a valid death recipient)\n- userspace sends BC_DEAD_BINDER_DONE while a clear was already pending\n\nUserspace needs to send these without reading from the kernel, so using a flushCommands(). Then, if userspace intiiates a transaction, thread-\u003etodo will not be empty.\n\nI think delivering these out of order is not a problem - in the first case it will return BR_ERROR and abort the process, in the other cases it results in a decWeak on a proxy object - delaying a decWeak() should be fine.\n\nA remote process should only be able to add to our thread-\u003etodo while we are waiting, so that should not be a problem either.\n\nDo you agree? If so we could also just remove the BUG_ON(). Perhaps Sherry\u0027s idea is safer - only add to _nowake if there\u0027s no work on thread-\u003etodo - I think this would not happen with normal libbinder usage.",
      "parentUuid": "e5b559a5_65b63508",
      "revId": "34c3493e45451d505d05c52266e946fbb592c001",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3650731_c0175d1f",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3289,
