      "message": "Actually, I don\u0027t think we can make it a user error, because this does happen in practice; libbinder already sends BC_REQUEST_DEATH_NOTIFICATION/BC_CLEAR_DEATH_NOTIFICATION with a flush(); it can\u0027t read from the kernel because the kernel doesn\u0027t always send something back in response.\n\nPS3 shows the flag; I think I prefer that solution, because it maintains the ordering no matter what (less fragile).",
